#
# Mon-Fri 4:55pm ET — warm the Back in Demand board for the DEFAULT universe
# (S&P 1500, ~1,500 names). Added 2026-08-14 when that became the landing tab
# on /supply-demand: the scan itself is fast (~7s) but the venue detail on the
# top rows costs a tape fetch each (~35s total), and the in-process cache is
# only 3h. Without this the first page view after a cache expiry eats the whole
# wait. Runs after the 4:50 pullback-scan so the price cache is already warm.
#
# OVER HTTP, NOT AS AN IMPORT (fixed 2026-08-15). demand_reentry's cache is a
# process-local dict, so `python -c "...d.scan()"` in THIS container warmed a
# cache that nothing ever reads and died with the process — the api container
# still cold-started on the first page view. Calling the endpoint makes the
# API warm its OWN memory. It answers instantly with warming:true and fills in
# a background thread, so the short timeout here is correct, not a truncation.
# X-User-Email satisfies require_auth_middleware; this port is internal to the
# compose network and never published.
55     16    *    *    1-5  curl -sS -m 30 -o /dev/null -w 'demand-reentry warm full: HTTP %{http_code}\n' -H 'X-User-Email: cron@internal' 'http://api:8000/supply-demand/demand-reentry?universe=full&limit=1'
